es-rgds-gamedetails: more about the game on the library's top screen (rating, players, developer, description, a screenshot)

The library's top screen showed a game's cover, its title, genre and year, the play stats and the achievements.
Themes for other frontends (Art Book Next, TechDweeb) also show the rating, the players, the developer and
publisher, the description, and a screenshot instead of the cover. The rnds engine now draws these in its own style:

- Under the genre and year, a row: the rating as five pixel stars (11 x 11 CSS px on the look's whole-pixel grid, by
  halves, in INK over LINE: the sheet is tinted with the system's accent, so accent stars vanished into it) and "1-2 players · Developer" (the publisher when there's no
  developer), cut with an ellipsis.
- Under the achievements, the description in MUTED, wrapped to 3 lines (2 under a two-line title, so the block stays
  clear of the help bar at the sheet's foot), the last cut with an ellipsis.
- The picture can be the gameplay screenshot (the metadata's image) instead of the box cover, in the same frame,
  shadow and shine. A game without a screenshot keeps its cover.

The block stays centred on the cover as before, its height grown by what is shown. The launch screen ("Starting...")
shows none of the extras.

Each is a setting, under USER INTERFACE SETTINGS with the theme's other switches (shown for the ROCKNIXDS Pixel
themes): TOP SCREEN ARTWORK (box art / screenshot, RndsTopArtwork), RATING STARS (RndsShowRating), PLAYERS AND
DEVELOPER (RndsShowCredits) and GAME DESCRIPTION (RndsShowDescription). The details are on by default and the
picture stays the box cover, so only the extras are new. The engine reads them as it draws, through new Source
virtuals (the host's defaults show everything and keep the cover), so a change shows without reloading the list.

